 > "scrn_update(): scp->end 0 > size_of_screen!!
 > scrn_update(): scp->start -1 < 0"
 > errors.
 > The weird thing the same cd worked well on the EB164.
 > The only difference between the two machine that the EB has no video card.
 > Could it be the problem?

Yes:

 > tga0: <DEC TGA2 (21130) 3D Graphics Accelerator> mem 0x88000000-0x88ffffff
 > irq 10 at device 13.0 on pci0
 > tga0: Board type (null)
 > tga0: 1024 x 0, 8bpp, IBM561 RAMDAC
 > tga0: interrupting at ISA irq 10
 > tga0: TGA2 (21130) pass 2

The TGA driver is mostly experimental.  And it is very poorly tested
except on TGA1 boards.

I think that the install should work just fine if you open the box and
remove the graphics card.

Sorry about that.

Drew

